# ============================================================
#  SSL setup (Let's Encrypt)
#  1) point senzskinshop.com A-record to your server IP
#  2) on the server run:
#       sudo apt install certbot
#       sudo certbot certonly --webroot -w /var/www/senzskinshop/nginx/acme \
#            -d senzskinshop.com -d www.senzskinshop.com \
#            --email info@senzskinshop.com --agree-tos --no-eff-email
#  3) copy the files into ./nginx/certs:
#       sudo cp /etc/letsencrypt/live/senzskinshop.com/fullchain.pem nginx/certs/
#       sudo cp /etc/letsencrypt/live/senzskinshop.com/privkey.pem  nginx/certs/
#  4) uncomment the HTTPS server block in nginx/default.conf and the
#     http→https redirect, then:  docker compose exec nginx nginx -s reload
#  5) auto-renew:  sudo certbot renew --deploy-hook "cd /var/www/senzskinshop && docker compose exec nginx nginx -s reload"
# ============================================================
